WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.920
If your prep is SuTab, this video will walk you through exactly how to take it.

2
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.160
Just follow along, step by step.

3
00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:10.400
Your SuTab kit includes two bottles of 12 tablets each and a measured container.

4
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:15.760
Start your first dose between 6 and 7 PM the night before your procedure.

5
00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:18.000
Open your first bottle of 12 tablets.

6
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.560
Fill the provided container with 16 ounces of water up to the fill line.

7
00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:27.040
Swallow one tablet every 2 minutes with a sip of water, finishing all 12

8
00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:27.680
tablets over

9
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:31.760
about 15 to 20 minutes. Take your time and go at a steady pace.

10
00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:37.690
About 1 hour after your last tablet, fill the container again with 16 ounces

11
00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:38.320
of water

12
00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:41.120
and drink the entire amount slowly over 30 minutes.

13
00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:45.920
Then, about 30 minutes after finishing that container, fill it one more time

14
00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:46.960
with 16 ounces

15
00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:51.660
of water and drink the entire amount over 30 minutes. That completes your first

16
00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:52.160
dose.

17
00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:57.150
7 hours prior to your procedure, repeat the exact same three steps using

18
00:00:57.150 --> 00:00:57.840
your second bottle

19
00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:02.510
of 12 tablets. One tablet every 2 minutes with water, then 16 ounces of water

20
00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:03.760
one hour later,

21
00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:06.400
then 16 ounces of water, 30 minutes after that.

22
00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:10.070
This part is really important. You must drink all of the prep solution as

23
00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:10.640
directed,

24
00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:12.640
even if you're already passing clear liquid.

25
00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:17.020
I know it can feel like enough, but finishing the entire dose is what gives us

26
00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:17.440
the clearest

27
00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:21.210
view during your procedure. If the prep isn't completed as directed, we may

28
00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:22.160
need to reschedule,

29
00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:26.270
and neither of us wants that. Between doses, keep drinking clear liquids to

30
00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:27.200
stay hydrated.

31
00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:29.680
It will help you feel better and help the prep do its job.

32
00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:34.810
Do not drink anything at all within 4 hours of your procedure, including

33
00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:35.440
water,

34
00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:37.760
unless it is a small sip to take a medication.

35
00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:42.000
Your procedure may be canceled or rescheduled if this is not followed.

36
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:45.600
If you experience any discomfort from frequent trips to the bathroom,

37
00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:49.840
applying a petroleum-based ointment or diaper rash cream can really help.

38
00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:54.320
That's it. You've got this. Follow the timing,

39
00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:58.720
finish the full dose, and stay hydrated. If you have any questions at all,

40
00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:02.640
don't hesitate to call our office. We're here to help.
